@bcoca @sivel @webknjaz Can you please have a look at this and let me know what it needs?

I personally find the whole idea of hard-wrapping to terminal reported width quite problematic as it fails to cover of CI/CD usage. At the time output is produced you do not always know what will be the width so is better to allow the terminal to do the soft-wrapping instead of behaving like a TUI/ncurses app that needs fixed size terminal.

Obviously that this means that this makes the start header padding problematic, so we should use a maximum value for it.

